01.Constructor
The constructor takes x, y and color and width. super() calls the constructor from the parent class and gets the x, y and color. And we also store the width in the object which is not inherited.

02.to string method
Here we return a string showing the coloredfigure data about the position and its color.

Class ColoredFigure

Coloredfigure inherits everything from figure class. And the coloredfigure is a type of figure

01.Constructor
The constructor takes x, y and color. super() calls the constructor from the parent class figure. And we also store the color in the object which is not inherited.

02.area method
This is a method to calculate the area which for a square is the width * width and returns it.

03.perimeter method
This is a method to calculate the perimeter which is width * 4 and returns it.

04.to string method
Here we return a string showing the figures data which is the coordinates x and y its width and its color and returns it.

After we finish with all the classes we have a cs variable which creates a new coloredsquare object. Sets x = 120, y = 80, width = 3 and color = red.
After that we move the square with 0 and -5 with the move method of the class.
So dx = 0 and dy = -5.
And finally we print the squares information (toString method), the area (area method) and perimemeter (perimeter method)
